title    phyllotaxis
date     2026-07-29
tags     maths nature form
stage    evergreen
src      /media/phyllotaxis.svg
alt      900 dots placed at successive golden-angle rotations, forming spiral arms
caption  900 points, each rotated 137.5° from the last.
---
The golden angle is `2π(1 − 1/φ)` ≈ 137.507°. Place seeds at successive
multiples of it, with radius growing as `√n`, and no two ever line up — which
is why sunflowers and pinecones do it.

This is an SVG, so it is text, it scales forever, and it weighs nothing next to
a photograph of the same thing.

> Later this becomes a wasm piece instead of a static file: the same maths in
> ~120 lines of C, drawing itself.
